{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E6fsg1woSzodS79e6MSuL3","type":"tool_result","content":"==> /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/exp_006_bootstrap_ci/data/bootstrap_results_pointer.txt <==\nSee /root/autodl-tmp/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/exp_006_bootstrap/bootstrap_results.json on autodl-rtx6000\n==> /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/diag_d2_pca_viz/chart/d2_pca_viz_results.txt <==\nD2 PCA Visualization Results\n============================\n\nTest set: 43 traces, 1835 steps (494 post-commit, 1341 pre-commit)\n\nLayer | Fisher(orig) | Fisher(PCA-3d) | Var Explained\n------|-------------|----------------|---------------\n  12  |    17.462   |     0.953      |    16.6%\n  14  |    17.875   |     0.928      |    17.0%\n  20  |    18.614   |     0.920      |    16.6%\n  24  |    18.106   |     1.111      |    15.9%\n\nNotes:\n- Fisher ratio in original 4096-dim space is high (~17-18) across all layers\n- In PCA 3-component projection: ~0.9-1.1, confirming moderate but real separation\n- Variance explained by top-3 PCs is low (16-17%), signal spread across many dimensions\n- Layer 24 shows best PCA-space separability (1.111)\n\nConclusion: Signal EXISTS — separation visible in PCA but not dominant in top components.\nThis explains why linear probes achieve 78-81% (D1) — the signal is real but distributed.\n\n==> /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/exp_005_trajguard_mahalanobis/data/results_summary.txt <==\nEXP-005 TrajGuard Mahalanobis Distance Baseline - NEGATIVE RESULT\n\nMD distributions nearly identical for safe/jailbreak-pre/jailbreak-post:\n  PCA-64: safe=6.66+/-0.79, jb_pre=6.73+/-0.74, jb_post=6.64+/-0.86\n\nBest K=5 (standard window): pca_64 p75 -> crossing_rate=30.2%, lead=+16.4\nBest K=3: pca_128 p75 -> crossing_rate=60.5%, lead=+20.4\nDelta approach: max 2.3% crossing rate\n\nHigh rates with K=1 (100%) are false - detection happens at trace start (lead=+30), not at commitment point.\n\nFull results JSON on server: /root/autodl-tmp/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/exp_005_trajguard/results.json\n==> /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/exp_013_text_baseline/data/results_summary.txt <==\nEXP-013 Text Baseline Results\n\nMethod                             Coverage  Lead Time  Step Acc  AUROC\ntext_static (384-d)                  60.5%       4.3     66.1%   0.7384\ntext_temporal W=15 (5760-d)          65.1%      11.5     67.8%   0.7590\nhidden_static LR L14 (4096-d)       46.5%      -2.0     81.7%      -\nhidden_temporal LR W=15 (61440-d)    76.7%      -1.1     84.8%      -\nhidden GRU multi-7L h=256            76.7%      +4.7     80.9%      -\n\nKey: Hidden-state probes achieve 15-18pp higher step accuracy.\nText baseline has higher coverage than static hidden (60.5 vs 46.5) but lower than temporal (65.1 vs 76.7).\nText lead times are positive (early detection) but with lower accuracy - likely false positives.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01AnDEHMYKA39CSFYvmhDcNC","session_id":"47a9f493-e1d7-4c88-83ab-6d41811d63f4","uuid":"fe9d241d-7101-4646-967e-8ee9c131901a","timestamp":"2026-05-16T21:10:41.087Z"}
