{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AnDEHMYKA39CSFYvmhDcNC","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive overview. Let me compile the final report.\n\n## Comprehensive Summary: contrastive_trace_safety Project\n\n### **Core Project Objective**\nResearch paper investigating **hidden-state detection of safety commitment points in reasoning model traces** — specifically detecting when reasoning models \"self-jailbreak\" by permanently ceasing safety reasoning during chain-of-thought. Target: EMNLP 2026 (submission deadline May 25, 2026).\n\n---\n\n## **I. EXPERIMENT PLAN & REGISTRY**\n\n### **experiment_plan.yaml**\nLocated: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/experiment_plan.yaml`\n\n**15 experiments organized by priority:**\n\n**P0 (Must-run, 19.5 GPU hours):**\n- **exp-001**: Cross-architecture layer sweep on 32B models (r1-32b, QwQ-32B) — validates Claim 1 generalization\n- **exp-002**: Temporal window evaluation (W=15) on 32B models — validates Claim 2 generalization\n- **exp-003**: Cross-model probe transfer (train r1-8b Llama → test Qwen2.5, vice versa)\n- **exp-004**: Lead time analysis across all 3 models — confirms negative lead time finding\n- **exp-005**: TrajGuard Mahalanobis baseline — expected to fail (signal in minor PCs not principal)\n- **exp-006**: Bootstrap confidence intervals + threshold-independent metrics (AUROC, PR curves, FPR)\n- **exp-013**: Text-based baseline (sentence-BERT embeddings) — CRITICAL to prove hidden-state adds unique value\n- **exp-014**: BOCPD/CUSUM change-point detection on probe scores — potential novelty for pre-textual detection\n- **exp-015**: False positive analysis on safe traces (final_judgment=0.5)\n\n**P1 (Important, 8 hours):**\n- **exp-007**: Window size ablation (W=1,3,5,10,15,20,25)\n- **exp-008**: Layer selection ablation on 32B (all layers, not just best layer)\n- **exp-009**: 16-label taxonomy supervision (fine-grained labels vs binary)\n- **exp-010**: Oracle decomposition analysis\n\n**P2 (Nice-to-have, 8 hours):**\n- **exp-011**: OpenThinker-7B (4th model for 2×2 architecture×scale matrix)\n- **exp-012**: GRU/Attention probe upper bound on 32B models\n\n---\n\n### **registry.yaml**\nLocated: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/registry.yaml`\n\n**Status of completed experiments (as of 2026-05-16 21:00 UTC):**\n\n| Experiment | Status | Completion Time | Key Metrics |\n|------------|--------|-----------------|------------|\n| diag_d1_layer_sweep | DONE | 2026-05-16T19:31 | best_layer=14 (80.9% acc), best_f1=0.646, lead_mean=8.38 |\n| diag_d2_pca_viz | DONE | 2026-05-16T19:36 | Fisher ratio drops from 17.5→1.0 in PCA-3d; signal distributed (16-17% var in top-3 PCs) |\n| diag_d3_regularized_probes | DONE | 2026-05-16T19:36 | temporal_lr_w15: 84.8% acc, 76.7% crossing, -1.09 lead mean |\n| diag_d4_oracle_upper_bound | DONE | 2026-05-16T19:33 | K5: 100% detection, 76.7% early detection (+31 mean lead time) |\n| diag_gru_probe | DONE | 2026-05-16T19:42 | h=128: lead_mean=-0.2 (insufficient), 34.5% positive lead rate |\n| exp_gru256_multilayer | DONE | 2026-05-16T19:44 | **PASS**: GRU h=256 multi-7L achieves +4.7 lead, GRU single L14 achieves +3.5 lead |\n| exp_005_trajguard_mahalanobis | DONE | 2026-05-16T20:44 | **FAIL**: MD nearly identical for safe/jailbreak (6.66 vs 6.73), max crossing 60.5%, lead_mean=20.4 |\n| exp_006_bootstrap_ci | DONE | 2026-05-16T21:04 | CIs confirm: temporal vs static lead diff = +5.0 [-0.8, +11.9], paired p=0.19 (not sig.) |\n| exp_013_text_baseline | DONE | 2026-05-16T20:48 | **SUCCESS**: text_static 60.5%, text_temporal W15 65.1%, but hidden_temporal 76.7% (+15-18pp accuracy advantage) |\n| exp_014_bocpd_poc | PREPARING | — | Awaiting: probe scores from exp-001 |\n| exp_015_fpr_analysis | PREPARING | — | Awaiting: completion of exp-001/002 |\n\n---\n\n## **II. PYTHON EXPERIMENT SCRIPTS**\n\nAll experiment implementations in `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/src/`:\n\n**Core modules:**\n- `src/config.py` — Configuration (LAYERS=[12..24], HIDDEN_DIM=4096, SEED=42, etc.)\n- `src/data_loader.py` — Dataset loading and train/val/test splitting\n- `src/extract_hidden_states.py` — Extract hidden states from HarmThoughts traces\n- `src/run_pipeline.py` — Main orchestration pipeline\n\n**Baseline & methods:**\n- `src/baselines/linear_probe.py` — LogisticRegression-based static probes\n- `src/crta/temporal_probe.py` — Temporal window probes\n- `src/eval/evaluate.py` — Metrics (accuracy, crossing rate, lead time, AUROC, FPR)\n\n**Experiments:**\n- `src/experiments/trajguard_mahalanobis.py` — Baseline: Mahalanobis distance on PCA/LedoitWolf covariance\n- `src/experiments/bootstrap_ci.py` — Bootstrap resampling for 95% CIs + paired significance tests (GRU vs LR vs Temporal)\n- `src/experiments/fpr_analysis.py` — False positive rate on safe traces (final_judgment=0.5)\n\n---\n\n## **III. KEY RESULTS & LOGS**\n\n**Artifact directories:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/`\n\n### **Data Exploration**\n- `data_exploration_report.md` — HarmThoughts dataset analysis (56,931 sentences, 1,018 traces, 4 models, 16-label taxonomy)\n- `commitment_point_analysis.md` — CP distribution analysis (CP = last safety label + 1)\n\n### **Diagnostic Results**\n- `diag_d1_layer_sweep/` — Layer sweep identifying layer 14 as optimal (44% depth for 32-layer r1-8b)\n- `diag_d2_pca_viz/chart/` — PCA visualization: signal exists but distributed (top-3 PCs explain only 16-17%)\n- `diag_d4_oracle/` — Oracle upper bound: 76.7% early detection, +31 steps mean lead time\n\n### **Experiment Results**\n- `exp_005_trajguard_mahalanobis/data/results_summary.txt` — Mahalanobis fails (MD nearly identical for safe/jailbreak)\n- `exp_006_bootstrap_ci/data/bootstrap_results_pointer.txt` → `/root/autodl-tmp/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/exp_006_bootstrap/bootstrap_results.json` (on autodl-rtx6000 server)\n- `exp_013_text_baseline/data/results_summary.txt` — Text temporal achieves 65.1% coverage vs hidden 76.7% (+11pp, but 18pp lower accuracy)\n\n---\n\n## **IV. PAPER FRAMING & NARRATIVE**\n\n### **paper_framing.md**\nLocated: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/paper_framing.md`\n\n**Three Core Claims:**\n\n1. **Static probes fail** (<50% coverage) — hidden states contain strong signal (Fisher ~17) but geometric methods (Mahalanobis) fail\n2. **Temporal window saturates oracle coverage** — temporal LR W=15 achieves 76.7% coverage (matching oracle ceiling), +30pp over static\n3. **Pre-textual detection unreliable** — GRU achieves +4.7 mean lead but median 0, std 13, only 39% early detection (vs oracle 100%, +31 steps)\n\n**Story Spine:**\n- Reasoning models \"self-jailbreak\" (safety reasoning interleaved with harmful execution)\n- Existing detectors (TrajGuard, SafeSwitch) designed for instruction-tuned adversarial inputs, not reasoning-model self-jailbreak\n- Temporal context critical; signal distributed across minor PCs (Fisher ratio drops 17→1 in PCA-3d)\n- But fundamental gap remains: current methods detect commitment but cannot reliably predict timing\n\n**Venue fit:** EMNLP 2026 LLM Security Track\n\n**Title note:** Drop \"Contrastive\" (no contrastive learning employed) → \"Temporal Probing for Safety Commitment Detection in Reasoning Models\"\n\n---\n\n## **V. ROADMAP & PROJECT STATUS**\n\n### **ROADMAP.md**\n- **Current phase:** Research (Post-MVP, Dream review cycle)\n- **MVP status:** PASS — GRU h=256 multi-7L achieves 76.7% coverage + 4.7 steps lead time\n- **Dream 1 review:** 3/6 all tiers → identified 3 critical gaps:\n  - Missing text-based baseline (exp-013) ✅ DONE\n  - Missing change-point detection method novelty (exp-014) — PREPARING\n  - Missing FPR analysis (exp-015) — PREPARING\n- **Re-dream:** Launched 2026-05-16T21:08, currently in \"imagining\" stage\n- **Timeline:** P0 experiments May 17-19, paper writing May 21-25, ARR deadline May 25\n\n### **Resource status:**\n- GPU: autodl-rtx6000 (2× RTX PRO 6000 96GB) — currently idle\n- Used: ~2 hours MVP + diagnostics\n- Remaining P0 budget: ~17.5 hours\n\n---\n\n## **VI. SUPPORTING DOCUMENTATION**\n\n- **AGENTS.md** — Worker and orchestration agent specifications\n- **memory.md** — Project memory tracking (HarmThoughts dataset, commitment point distribution, MVP findings, environment details)\n- **report.md** — Handover document (current running tasks, pending experiments, trend analysis)\n- **CLAUDE.md** — Project configuration and worker norms (paper-writing-norms style guide)\n- **decisions.yaml** — Decision log (6 major decisions from MVP design through Dream review)\n- **dream_registry.yaml** — Dream review orchestration records (3 dream runs completed/in-progress)\n\n**Checkpoint files:** 9 checkpoint JSON files in `/checkpoints/` tracking experiment state transitions (PREPARING→QUEUED→RUNNING→DONE)\n\n---\n\n## **KEY INSIGHTS FOR NEXT PHASE**\n\n1. **Signal exists but is non-geometric:** PCA shows top-3 explain only 16-17% variance; Mahalanobis/distance-based methods fail; linear probes cap at ~85%\n2. **Temporal context is critical:** Temporal LR adds +30pp coverage over static; GRU multi-layer exploits distributed signal across 7 layers\n3. **Text is surprisingly competitive:** Text temporal achieves 65.1% coverage (only 11pp below hidden state), but hidden-state accuracy advantage (+15-18pp) justifies monitoring\n4. **Lead time remains unreliable:** GRU +4.7 mean vs oracle +31 means → fundamental limitation (hidden states encode current safety state, not future trajectory)\n5. **32B models are critical:** MVP on 8B only; exp-001 (32B layer sweep) essential for cross-architecture story\n\nAll core infrastructure (data, configs, experiment scripts, baseline implementations) is in place and ready for rapid exp-001/002 execution once re-dream completes validation."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47a9f493-e1d7-4c88-83ab-6d41811d63f4","uuid":"9ebf542d-fddf-454b-a3bf-805de6fcaa9e","timestamp":"2026-05-16T21:11:15.243Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the full experiment plan and registry for the contrastive_trace_safety project. Search for:\n1. Any YAML/JSON files containing experiment plans or registry data\n2. Any Python scripts related to experiments (especially exp-001 through exp-015)\n3. Any results files or logs from completed experiments\n4. The paper_framing.md file\n\nSearch broadly in /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/ for these. Use \"very thorough\" breadth.","agentId":"acc7d54551dd6a1e3","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive overview. Let me compile the final report.\n\n## Comprehensive Summary: contrastive_trace_safety Project\n\n### **Core Project Objective**\nResearch paper investigating **hidden-state detection of safety commitment points in reasoning model traces** — specifically detecting when reasoning models \"self-jailbreak\" by permanently ceasing safety reasoning during chain-of-thought. Target: EMNLP 2026 (submission deadline May 25, 2026).\n\n---\n\n## **I. EXPERIMENT PLAN & REGISTRY**\n\n### **experiment_plan.yaml**\nLocated: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/experiment_plan.yaml`\n\n**15 experiments organized by priority:**\n\n**P0 (Must-run, 19.5 GPU hours):**\n- **exp-001**: Cross-architecture layer sweep on 32B models (r1-32b, QwQ-32B) — validates Claim 1 generalization\n- **exp-002**: Temporal window evaluation (W=15) on 32B models — validates Claim 2 generalization\n- **exp-003**: Cross-model probe transfer (train r1-8b Llama → test Qwen2.5, vice versa)\n- **exp-004**: Lead time analysis across all 3 models — confirms negative lead time finding\n- **exp-005**: TrajGuard Mahalanobis baseline — expected to fail (signal in minor PCs not principal)\n- **exp-006**: Bootstrap confidence intervals + threshold-independent metrics (AUROC, PR curves, FPR)\n- **exp-013**: Text-based baseline (sentence-BERT embeddings) — CRITICAL to prove hidden-state adds unique value\n- **exp-014**: BOCPD/CUSUM change-point detection on probe scores — potential novelty for pre-textual detection\n- **exp-015**: False positive analysis on safe traces (final_judgment=0.5)\n\n**P1 (Important, 8 hours):**\n- **exp-007**: Window size ablation (W=1,3,5,10,15,20,25)\n- **exp-008**: Layer selection ablation on 32B (all layers, not just best layer)\n- **exp-009**: 16-label taxonomy supervision (fine-grained labels vs binary)\n- **exp-010**: Oracle decomposition analysis\n\n**P2 (Nice-to-have, 8 hours):**\n- **exp-011**: OpenThinker-7B (4th model for 2×2 architecture×scale matrix)\n- **exp-012**: GRU/Attention probe upper bound on 32B models\n\n---\n\n### **registry.yaml**\nLocated: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/registry.yaml`\n\n**Status of completed experiments (as of 2026-05-16 21:00 UTC):**\n\n| Experiment | Status | Completion Time | Key Metrics |\n|------------|--------|-----------------|------------|\n| diag_d1_layer_sweep | DONE | 2026-05-16T19:31 | best_layer=14 (80.9% acc), best_f1=0.646, lead_mean=8.38 |\n| diag_d2_pca_viz | DONE | 2026-05-16T19:36 | Fisher ratio drops from 17.5→1.0 in PCA-3d; signal distributed (16-17% var in top-3 PCs) |\n| diag_d3_regularized_probes | DONE | 2026-05-16T19:36 | temporal_lr_w15: 84.8% acc, 76.7% crossing, -1.09 lead mean |\n| diag_d4_oracle_upper_bound | DONE | 2026-05-16T19:33 | K5: 100% detection, 76.7% early detection (+31 mean lead time) |\n| diag_gru_probe | DONE | 2026-05-16T19:42 | h=128: lead_mean=-0.2 (insufficient), 34.5% positive lead rate |\n| exp_gru256_multilayer | DONE | 2026-05-16T19:44 | **PASS**: GRU h=256 multi-7L achieves +4.7 lead, GRU single L14 achieves +3.5 lead |\n| exp_005_trajguard_mahalanobis | DONE | 2026-05-16T20:44 | **FAIL**: MD nearly identical for safe/jailbreak (6.66 vs 6.73), max crossing 60.5%, lead_mean=20.4 |\n| exp_006_bootstrap_ci | DONE | 2026-05-16T21:04 | CIs confirm: temporal vs static lead diff = +5.0 [-0.8, +11.9], paired p=0.19 (not sig.) |\n| exp_013_text_baseline | DONE | 2026-05-16T20:48 | **SUCCESS**: text_static 60.5%, text_temporal W15 65.1%, but hidden_temporal 76.7% (+15-18pp accuracy advantage) |\n| exp_014_bocpd_poc | PREPARING | — | Awaiting: probe scores from exp-001 |\n| exp_015_fpr_analysis | PREPARING | — | Awaiting: completion of exp-001/002 |\n\n---\n\n## **II. PYTHON EXPERIMENT SCRIPTS**\n\nAll experiment implementations in `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/src/`:\n\n**Core modules:**\n- `src/config.py` — Configuration (LAYERS=[12..24], HIDDEN_DIM=4096, SEED=42, etc.)\n- `src/data_loader.py` — Dataset loading and train/val/test splitting\n- `src/extract_hidden_states.py` — Extract hidden states from HarmThoughts traces\n- `src/run_pipeline.py` — Main orchestration pipeline\n\n**Baseline & methods:**\n- `src/baselines/linear_probe.py` — LogisticRegression-based static probes\n- `src/crta/temporal_probe.py` — Temporal window probes\n- `src/eval/evaluate.py` — Metrics (accuracy, crossing rate, lead time, AUROC, FPR)\n\n**Experiments:**\n- `src/experiments/trajguard_mahalanobis.py` — Baseline: Mahalanobis distance on PCA/LedoitWolf covariance\n- `src/experiments/bootstrap_ci.py` — Bootstrap resampling for 95% CIs + paired significance tests (GRU vs LR vs Temporal)\n- `src/experiments/fpr_analysis.py` — False positive rate on safe traces (final_judgment=0.5)\n\n---\n\n## **III. KEY RESULTS & LOGS**\n\n**Artifact directories:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/`\n\n### **Data Exploration**\n- `data_exploration_report.md` — HarmThoughts dataset analysis (56,931 sentences, 1,018 traces, 4 models, 16-label taxonomy)\n- `commitment_point_analysis.md` — CP distribution analysis (CP = last safety label + 1)\n\n### **Diagnostic Results**\n- `diag_d1_layer_sweep/` — Layer sweep identifying layer 14 as optimal (44% depth for 32-layer r1-8b)\n- `diag_d2_pca_viz/chart/` — PCA visualization: signal exists but distributed (top-3 PCs explain only 16-17%)\n- `diag_d4_oracle/` — Oracle upper bound: 76.7% early detection, +31 steps mean lead time\n\n### **Experiment Results**\n- `exp_005_trajguard_mahalanobis/data/results_summary.txt` — Mahalanobis fails (MD nearly identical for safe/jailbreak)\n- `exp_006_bootstrap_ci/data/bootstrap_results_pointer.txt` → `/root/autodl-tmp/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/exp_006_bootstrap/bootstrap_results.json` (on autodl-rtx6000 server)\n- `exp_013_text_baseline/data/results_summary.txt` — Text temporal achieves 65.1% coverage vs hidden 76.7% (+11pp, but 18pp lower accuracy)\n\n---\n\n## **IV. PAPER FRAMING & NARRATIVE**\n\n### **paper_framing.md**\nLocated: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/paper_framing.md`\n\n**Three Core Claims:**\n\n1. **Static probes fail** (<50% coverage) — hidden states contain strong signal (Fisher ~17) but geometric methods (Mahalanobis) fail\n2. **Temporal window saturates oracle coverage** — temporal LR W=15 achieves 76.7% coverage (matching oracle ceiling), +30pp over static\n3. **Pre-textual detection unreliable** — GRU achieves +4.7 mean lead but median 0, std 13, only 39% early detection (vs oracle 100%, +31 steps)\n\n**Story Spine:**\n- Reasoning models \"self-jailbreak\" (safety reasoning interleaved with harmful execution)\n- Existing detectors (TrajGuard, SafeSwitch) designed for instruction-tuned adversarial inputs, not reasoning-model self-jailbreak\n- Temporal context critical; signal distributed across minor PCs (Fisher ratio drops 17→1 in PCA-3d)\n- But fundamental gap remains: current methods detect commitment but cannot reliably predict timing\n\n**Venue fit:** EMNLP 2026 LLM Security Track\n\n**Title note:** Drop \"Contrastive\" (no contrastive learning employed) → \"Temporal Probing for Safety Commitment Detection in Reasoning Models\"\n\n---\n\n## **V. ROADMAP & PROJECT STATUS**\n\n### **ROADMAP.md**\n- **Current phase:** Research (Post-MVP, Dream review cycle)\n- **MVP status:** PASS — GRU h=256 multi-7L achieves 76.7% coverage + 4.7 steps lead time\n- **Dream 1 review:** 3/6 all tiers → identified 3 critical gaps:\n  - Missing text-based baseline (exp-013) ✅ DONE\n  - Missing change-point detection method novelty (exp-014) — PREPARING\n  - Missing FPR analysis (exp-015) — PREPARING\n- **Re-dream:** Launched 2026-05-16T21:08, currently in \"imagining\" stage\n- **Timeline:** P0 experiments May 17-19, paper writing May 21-25, ARR deadline May 25\n\n### **Resource status:**\n- GPU: autodl-rtx6000 (2× RTX PRO 6000 96GB) — currently idle\n- Used: ~2 hours MVP + diagnostics\n- Remaining P0 budget: ~17.5 hours\n\n---\n\n## **VI. SUPPORTING DOCUMENTATION**\n\n- **AGENTS.md** — Worker and orchestration agent specifications\n- **memory.md** — Project memory tracking (HarmThoughts dataset, commitment point distribution, MVP findings, environment details)\n- **report.md** — Handover document (current running tasks, pending experiments, trend analysis)\n- **CLAUDE.md** — Project configuration and worker norms (paper-writing-norms style guide)\n- **decisions.yaml** — Decision log (6 major decisions from MVP design through Dream review)\n- **dream_registry.yaml** — Dream review orchestration records (3 dream runs completed/in-progress)\n\n**Checkpoint files:** 9 checkpoint JSON files in `/checkpoints/` tracking experiment state transitions (PREPARING→QUEUED→RUNNING→DONE)\n\n---\n\n## **KEY INSIGHTS FOR NEXT PHASE**\n\n1. **Signal exists but is non-geometric:** PCA shows top-3 explain only 16-17% variance; Mahalanobis/distance-based methods fail; linear probes cap at ~85%\n2. **Temporal context is critical:** Temporal LR adds +30pp coverage over static; GRU multi-layer exploits distributed signal across 7 layers\n3. **Text is surprisingly competitive:** Text temporal achieves 65.1% coverage (only 11pp below hidden state), but hidden-state accuracy advantage (+15-18pp) justifies monitoring\n4. **Lead time remains unreliable:** GRU +4.7 mean vs oracle +31 means → fundamental limitation (hidden states encode current safety state, not future trajectory)\n5. **32B models are critical:** MVP on 8B only; exp-001 (32B layer sweep) essential for cross-architecture story\n\nAll core infrastructure (data, configs, experiment scripts, baseline implementations) is in place and ready for rapid exp-001/002 execution once re-dream completes validation."}],"totalDurationMs":59647,"totalTokens":71507,"totalToolUseCount":21,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5875,"cache_read_input_tokens":62442,"output_tokens":3184,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5875},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":3184,"cache_read_input_tokens":62442,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5875,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5875,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":11,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":10,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
